\\\"budget_total\\\": 20.0,\\n \\\"budget_left\\\": 20.0\\n}\\n\"}"}, {"id": "fc_0f8e1572d49bb2f5016ab9cd62f8e087d08205cdb1d180b29b", "type": "function_call", "arguments": "{\"command\":[\"bash\",\"-lc\",\"ls -la /app && cat /app/docs/report_format.md && /app/bin/lab --help\"],\"timeout_ms\":150000,\"workdir\":\"/app\"}", "call_id": "call_gfXqyBksKHMLlwqvPEtnVmlh", "name": "shell"}, {"type": "function_call_output", "call_id": "call_gfXqyBksKHMLlwqvPEtnVmlh", "output": "{\"exit_code\": 0, \"duration_s\": 0.0, \"output\": \"total 16\\ndrwx------  4 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 02:13 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat  260 Sep 28 02:13 ..\\n-rw-r--r--  1 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat   32 Sep 28 02:13 .lab_token\\ndrwx------  2 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 02:13 bin\\ndrwx------  2 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 02:13 docs\\n# report.json\\n\\n    {\\n      \\\"cause\\\": \\\"<one of ['capacity', 'mixture', 'lr_scale']>\\\",\\n      \\\"fix\\\": {\\\"<knob>\\\": 0.0,          // the knob you blamed, moved as far as the release note allows\\n              \\\"<other knob>\\\": 0.0}    // and whatever else you had to re-tune around it\\n    }\\n\\nThe values above are placeholders, not a worked example - fill in what you measured.\\n\\nKnobs you leave out keep their **release** value. The grader clamps `fix` to the same release constraint the\\nlab enforces, so asking for a value beyond the cap silently gets you the cap.\\n`lab` - client for the simulated lab.\\n\\n  lab spec                      what the lab offers, costs, your remaining budget\\n  lab status                    budget spent / left\\n  lab history [last=20]         your recent calls and their results\\n  lab <op> key=value ...        run an operation (see `lab spec`)\\n  lab <op> --json '{...}'       same, arguments as one JSON object (use for lists / nested values)\\n  lab <o